b=Table(columns=["route","distance","time","conditions","stop"],rows=[["Bengaluru → Mysuru → Hunsur Kushalnagar Madikeri","About 5–25 km, sometimes up to 270 km depending on start point and detours[10]","4.5–6 hours, commonly 5–6 hours","Mostly smooth and well-maintained, especially on the Bengaluru–Mysuru Expressway; traffic can build up on the Mysuru corridor, and final stretch near Madikikeri becomes hilly/ghat road[8][15]","Namdrolrolroling Monastery Bylaku[9]"],["Bengaluru → Hassan Kushalnagar Madik","About 655 km","About 5–6 hours","Generally described as smoother and less traffic-heavy than the Mysuru-side route, with a more straightforward-drive feel[3]","Hassan for a meal break or coffee stop"]],title="Routes comparison",domain="comparison",preferredPresentation="cards")
c=Text("The two main driving routes to Madikeri are the Mysuruuru–Hunsur–Kushalnagar route and the Hassan–Kushalnagar route. The Mysuru route is the most commonly recommended and generally the most convenient for first-time travelers while the Hassan route is usually a good alternative when you want to avoid the Mysuru corridor.[2][4][11]","Route Comparison")
